c0ab195fde5e12559ca72c71e1624e0b3c21bbf7:skills/red-ink/SKILL.md:3:description: "Present an existing design back to its owner in rounds until they say they are happy: copy the design first (original untouched), walk output first, then system inputs, then internals (data, state, functions, names, concepts); every round is Observe (teach) -> Orient (what matters) -> Decide (one detailed question, the owner's call) -> Act (one settled edit to the copy), closing with an IIUC playback and, at the end, a red chair of the settled design plus a decision record and proposed nodes (critical/major red-chair concerns appended as nodes). Use for Socratic design review of an existing artifact. Not for one-shot adversarial review (red-chair), authoring a new design (design), or interviewing an unclear request (ask, grill)."
c0ab195fde5e12559ca72c71e1624e0b3c21bbf7:skills/red-ink/SKILL.md:37:    return exit_pack(decisions, open_questions, nodes, chair)
c0ab195fde5e12559ca72c71e1624e0b3c21bbf7:skills/red-ink/SKILL.md:53:for elegant internals. One question per round keeps decisions
c0ab195fde5e12559ca72c71e1624e0b3c21bbf7:skills/red-ink/SKILL.md:82:| the request itself is unclear | `ask` / `grill` |
c0ab195fde5e12559ca72c71e1624e0b3c21bbf7:skills/red-ink/SKILL.md:92:| Slice | Question it answers |
c0ab195fde5e12559ca72c71e1624e0b3c21bbf7:skills/red-ink/SKILL.md:110:| Orient | the 2-4 things that matter, tensions, the turning question |
c0ab195fde5e12559ca72c71e1624e0b3c21bbf7:skills/red-ink/SKILL.md:111:| Decide | exactly one detailed question: options + recommended answer. The owner calls it |
c0ab195fde5e12559ca72c71e1624e0b3c21bbf7:skills/red-ink/SKILL.md:125:| Decide question still unanswered | stay on the slice |
c0ab195fde5e12559ca72c71e1624e0b3c21bbf7:skills/red-ink/SKILL.md:126:| owner defers a question | record it under Deliberately open, with an owner; move on only when the owner says so |
c0ab195fde5e12559ca72c71e1624e0b3c21bbf7:skills/red-ink/SKILL.md:139:| 4 | Deliberately open | deferred questions, each with an owner or an icebox path; plus icebox entries consulted at walk start |
